s JICA demand forecasts and an NEA-capacity ledger as transcribed in the notebook, with explicit synthetic demand, wet/dry hydro, solar PV, daily PROR pondage and monthly reservoir balances. Hydro classifications, plant CODs, technology costs and detailed measured hourly resource data remain unverified; BESS, transmission constraints and probabilistic EENS are excluded.","public_payload":{"model_version":"2030-evidence-first-notebook-v1","notebook_url":"https://github.com/aayush-bhatta/nepal-gep-workspace/blob/main/research/2030/Nepal_GEP_2030_Complete_Evidence_First.ipynb","methodology":"Source/assumption ledger → source-aware hourly proxy → LP with water and reliability constraints → HiGHS solution → 12 validation checks","source_urls":["https://openjicareport.jica.go.jp/pdf/12387999_01.pdf","https://www.nea.org.np/en/detail/annual-report-20252026"],"limits":["1,077.481 MW existing hydro unclassified","904.600 MW IPP classification provisional","2040 CF proxies for 2030 hydrology","288 representative optimized hours, reconstructed 8,760","Embedded cost benchmarks, not externally mounted CSV","No BESS, 2040/2050 output, probabilistic LOLE/EENS, or network flows"]}}]'::jsonb) as x(title text,kind text,summary text,public_payload jsonb))
